#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:9
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"Teach agents how to silently evaluate whether a work session produced "
"knowledge worth capturing, and if so, persist it without prompting the "
"user. This is the \"smart auto-capture\" skill — it only fires when "
"there's actually something to capture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:13
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:15
msgid ""
"This skill is embedded in the final step of `/deliver`, `/diagnose`, "
"`/retro`, and `/design`. You don't load it manually — it activates "
"automatically at the end of these workflows when `knowledge.auto_capture`"
" is enabled in `hero.json` (default: on)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:17
msgid "The decision: capture or skip?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"Before writing anything, evaluate whether the session produced **novel, "
"reusable knowledge**. Ask yourself:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:21
msgid "Capture if ANY of these are true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:22
msgid ""
"A technical constraint was discovered that isn't documented (e.g., \"FTS5"
" can't handle hyphens in MATCH queries\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:23
msgid ""
"A design decision was made with trade-offs discussed (e.g., \"chose SSE "
"over WebSockets for MCP transport\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:24
msgid ""
"A pattern was established that future work should follow (e.g., \"all CLI"
" flags use package-level vars and resetFlags()\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:25
msgid ""
"A workaround was needed for a tool/library limitation (e.g., \"Cobra flag"
" state persists across test runs\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:26
msgid ""
"An integration or API behavior was learned empirically (e.g., \"Figma API"
" can't generate designs, only read them\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:27
msgid ""
"A architectural boundary or constraint was established (e.g., \"no new Go"
" dependencies\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:29
msgid "Skip if ALL of these are true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:30
msgid "The work was straightforward implementation of an existing spec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:31
msgid "No surprises or unexpected behavior was encountered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:32
msgid "No decisions were made — just execution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:33
msgid "The knowledge already exists in `.hero/knowledge/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:35
msgid "When in doubt, skip. Noise in the knowledge base is worse than gaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:37
msgid "How to capture silently"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:39
msgid "When you determine something is worth capturing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:41
msgid "**Don't prompt the user.** Don't ask \"should I save this?\" Just do it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:42
msgid "**Classify the learning** into the right knowledge type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:43
msgid "Pattern/style → convention (`.hero/knowledge/conventions/<slug>/spec.md`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:44
msgid "Technical choice → decision (`.hero/knowledge/decisions/<slug>/spec.md`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:45
msgid "Hard constraint → rule (`.hero/knowledge/rules/<slug>/spec.md`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:46
msgid "Background info → context (`.hero/knowledge/context/<slug>/spec.md`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:47
msgid "Rough insight → note (`hero note <slug>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:49
msgid "**Write concisely.** Knowledge entries should be scannable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:50
msgid ""
"Title: clear, specific (not \"Database Notes\" — instead \"SQLite FTS5 "
"Hyphen Handling\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:51
msgid "Body: 3-10 sentences. What, why, and how to apply it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:52
msgid "Tags: 2-4 relevant tags for discoverability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:54
msgid ""
"**Mention it briefly at the end of your response.** One line, not a sales"
" pitch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:55
msgid "\"Captured convention: sqlite-fts5-hyphen-handling\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:56
msgid "\"Captured decision: sse-over-websockets-mcp-transport\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:57
msgid "Or if nothing: say nothing. Don't announce \"no knowledge captured.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:59
msgid "**Run `hero index`** after writing to make it searchable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:61
msgid "Knowledge entry templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:63
msgid "Convention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:64
msgid ""
"---\n"
"title: <Pattern Name>\n"
"type: convention\n"
"status: active\n"
"tags: [<tag1>, <tag2>]\n"
"created: <YYYY-MM-DD>\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Convention\n"
"\n"
"<What the pattern is. 1-2 sentences.>\n"
"\n"
"## Rationale\n"
"\n"
"<Why this pattern exists. What goes wrong without it.>\n"
"\n"
"## Examples\n"
"\n"
"<Good and bad examples if helpful.>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:86
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:87
msgid ""
"---\n"
"title: <Decision Title>\n"
"type: decision\n"
"status: accepted\n"
"tags: [<tag1>, <tag2>]\n"
"created: <YYYY-MM-DD>\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Decision\n"
"\n"
"<What was decided. 1 sentence.>\n"
"\n"
"## Context\n"
"\n"
"<What prompted this decision.>\n"
"\n"
"## Alternatives Considered\n"
"\n"
"<What else was evaluated and why it was rejected.>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:109
msgid "Rule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:110
msgid ""
"---\n"
"title: <Rule Name>\n"
"type: rule\n"
"status: active\n"
"tags: [<tag1>, <tag2>]\n"
"created: <YYYY-MM-DD>\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Rule\n"
"\n"
"<The constraint. 1 sentence.>\n"
"\n"
"## Rationale\n"
"\n"
"<Why this rule exists.>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:128
msgid "Deduplication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:130
msgid ""
"Before writing, mentally check against existing knowledge. If you recall "
"that a similar convention or decision already exists from earlier in the "
"conversation or from reading the knowledge base, don't create a "
"duplicate. If the existing entry needs updating, update it instead of "
"creating a new one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:132
msgid "Volume control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/auto-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md:134
msgid ""
"A typical session should produce 0-3 knowledge entries. If you find "
"yourself wanting to write more than 3, you're probably being too "
"granular. Consolidate related learnings into a single entry."
msgstr ""

